ed_at":"2026-10-24T07:29:21-04:00"}],"images":[{"id":48883291390183,"created_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:16-05:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:57-05:00","product_id":8559885943015,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0579\/8045\/3021\/files\/fuckery-heartland-black-hooded-coat-back.png?v=1768483137","width":1321,"height":1302},{"id":48883291422951,"created_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:16-05:00","position":2,"updated_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:57-05:00","product_id":8559885943015,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0579\/8045\/3021\/files\/fuckery-heartland-black-hooded-coat.png?v=1768483137","width":1321,"height":1302},{"id":48818765496551,"created_at":"2026-01-06T17:56:15-05:00","position":3,"updated_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:57-05:00","product_id":8559885943015,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0579\/8045\/3021\/files\/fuckeryheartland-hooded-coat.png?v=1768483137","width":1321,"height":1302},{"id":44505125486823,"created_at":"2025-02-13T00:51:40-05:00","position":4,"updated_at":"2026-01-15T08:18:57-05:00","product_id":8559885943015,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0579\/8045\/3021\/files\/2.2.25_2936_1.jpg?v=1768483137","width":5616,"height":3744}],"options":[{"name":"Size","position":1,"values":["Small","Medium","Large","X-Large","XX-Large","XXX-Large"]}]},{"id":8559848849639,"title":"New York City Arteries Gasoline Jackets","handle":"arteries-patch-on-gasoline-jacket","body_html":"\u003cp\u003e \u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNew York City Arteries was born on the Union Square L train platform, inspired by the giant subway map that once hung there. Walking past it daily, PJ found more than inspiration—those subway lines quite literally kept him alive. Selling prints \u0026amp; sketching underground built his independence, street smarts, \u0026amp; discipline in a way only New York could.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe design reshapes the NYC subway system into a human heart, with trains acting as blood pumping through the city’s veins—a tribute to the city’s pulse \u0026amp; survival.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Gasoline Jacket is built for real use, not decoration. Heavy-duty construction, reinforced stitching, \u0026amp; rugged materials make it dependable in daily wear, cold weather, \u0026amp; unpredictable conditions. Designed with utility in mind, it delivers warmth without bulk, freedom of movement, \u0026amp; long-term durability—made to be worn hard \u0026amp; trusted everywhere.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe New York City Arteries embroidery is on the back, placed boldly at the center of the upper shoulders, with a PJ O’Rourke signature embroidery on the left chest \u0026amp; a smaller Arteries embroidery beneath it. Dense stitching \u0026amp; high thread count give the artwork lasting depth \u0026amp; presence.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eMaterial-\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 12 oz. super-duty cotton duck\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Heavyweight fleece lined\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eFeatures-\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Pleated elbows and action back\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Two angled welt pockets\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Right-chest zipper pocket\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Three inside chest pockets\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Triple-needle stitched main seems\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Adjustable snap cuffs and side tabs\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eSizes: S - 3XL\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e*Note: 4XL not available.\u003c